  "id": "COMPOUND:18812 - PROTEIN:5814",
  "verbalization": "Homaxisterol A2 is implicated in the biological pathway leading to VMRC-MELG through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Homaxisterol A2 acts as a target for SNU-387, which in turn is targeted by Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside and Thelephantin K. These compounds are all linked to VMRC-MELG as their targets. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where Homaxisterol A2 may influence VMRC-MELG through the activation of SNU-387, which is a key player in the pathway. The shared target VMRC-MELG suggests a possible functional relationship between these compounds, possibly through a common downstream effect. The evidence supports a direct or indirect link between Homaxisterol A2 and VMRC-MELG, mediated by SNU-387 and its related compounds.",
